# EUReadySeller Live Verification

Do not rely on local-only checks when confirming a change.

## Required public checks
For every changed page, verify via public curl or equivalent live request:
- HTTP 200
- H1/title expected
- canonical trailing slash
- required phrases present
- forbidden phrases absent
- internal links present
- no cross-project contamination
- sitemap.xml includes the changed/new page
- llms.txt includes the changed/new page

## Cache-busting
Use a cache-busting query string for live checks:
- `?smoke=TIMESTAMP`

## URL hygiene checks when relevant
Also verify:
- `http` redirects to `https`
- non-trailing-slash redirects to trailing slash
- trailing-slash canonical returns 200

## Rule of evidence
If public live checks disagree with local checks, trust the public live result and investigate further.
